WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.991
The paper builds its data from scratch.

00:00:04.071 --> 00:00:08.062
Using OpenStreetMap road networks and the Google
Street View API,

00:00:08.142 --> 00:00:12.132
the authors sample points every four thousand
meters across the top global cities,

00:00:12.212 --> 00:00:16.203
collecting more than one hundred thirty thousand
geo-tagged street views spanning seventy-two

00:00:16.283 --> 00:00:20.274
cities in forty-eight countries.

00:00:20.354 --> 00:00:24.345
Applying the locatability filter at a threshold of
zero point four yields roughly seventy

00:00:24.425 --> 00:00:28.415
thousand high-quality images.

00:00:28.495 --> 00:00:32.486
Separately,

00:00:32.566 --> 00:00:36.557
they scrape over three thousand textual clues from
two geo-localization games,

00:00:36.637 --> 00:00:40.628
GeoGuessr and Tuxun,

00:00:40.708 --> 00:00:44.698
cleaning them with a BERT-based entity recognizer
and pairing each with a street-view image.

00:00:44.778 --> 00:00:48.769
For evaluation they use a held-out set of a
thousand images and,

00:00:48.849 --> 00:00:52.840
to test generalization, the standard Im2GPS and
Im2GPS3k Flickr benchmarks.
